course: dictionary
lesson: 14858
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Ratatouille is one of these words. «Grandma made a big pot of ratatouille for supper.» The words pot, supper and cooking show that ratatouille is food.
explain: «We watched Ratatouille on Friday night, and Remy the rat was so funny.» Now the clues are watched, Remy and funny. Ratatouille is the name of a film, and it has a capital R because it is a title.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here, a dish or a film? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. «We watched the stew on Friday night» does not make sense, so the film meaning is the right one here.
fact: Ratatouille is a French vegetable stew. It is made by slowly cooking tomatoes, courgettes (zucchini), aubergines (eggplants), peppers, onions and garlic in olive oil.
fact: Ratatouille is a noun, and it is usually uncountable, so you say «some ratatouille» or «a bowl of ratatouille», not «a ratatouille».
fact: «Ratatouille» is also the name of a 2007 Pixar film about a rat called Remy who wants to be a chef in Paris.
fact: Say it «rat-a-TOO-ee», with the stress on the middle part.
fact: Ratatouille is a healthy dish from Provence in the south of France, and it can be eaten hot or cold.
exercise: «Grandma made a big pot of ratatouille for supper.» What is ratatouille in this sentence? | A loud noise | A kind of hat | *A vegetable stew | A type of car
exercise: «We watched Ratatouille on Friday night, and Remy the rat was so funny.» What is Ratatouille in this sentence? | A vegetable | *A film | A French town | A kind of bread
exercise: Which vegetables go into ratatouille? | *Tomatoes and peppers | Fish and rice | Bananas and grapes | Sugar and chocolate
test: What is ratatouille cooked in? | Milk | Butter | Honey | *Olive oil
test: Ella says ratatouille can only be eaten hot. What is the truth? | It can only be eaten cold | It can only be eaten at Christmas | *It can be eaten hot or cold | It is a kind of cake
exam: Which sentence uses ratatouille as the name of a film? | «The ratatouille was still warm on the plate.» | «Mum cooked ratatouille in olive oil.» | «Ratatouille is a healthy dish from the south of France.» | *«We watched Ratatouille, the Pixar film, last night.»
